  {
    "runtag": "cfda-chiq-llm4cs-splade-rrf",
    "type": "ikat-dialog-v1",
    "topic": "2-2",
    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019m looking for some wine suggestions. Can you help me pick something interesting?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some wine suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Here are some interesting wine suggestions you might enjoy:\n\n1. **Chardonnay** - A versatile choice with a fruity flavor, perfect for pairing with dishes like chicken and pasta. Look for options like the Chablis Grand Cru, \"Les Clos\" Jean Marc Brocard (2009) for a premium experience.\n\n2. **Pinot Noir** - Known for its smooth texture and berry flavors, this wine pairs well with a variety of dishes, including mushroom and chicken ravioli. Try the Pinot Noir Grand Reserve, Josephine Dubois (2010).\n\n3. **Grenache** - A less acidic red that offers a fruity profile, great for those who prefer something smoother. Consider the Grenache from Ballast Stone, Currency Creek (2003).\n\n4. **Sauvignon Blanc** - Crisp and refreshing, ideal for lighter meals like salads or seafood. The Sancerre, Jean Vincent (2013) is a great pick.\n\n5. **Tempranillo** - A bold red wine with rich flavors, perfect for hearty dishes. Try the Tempranillo, Valdechate (2001) for something unique.\n\nThese wines provide a range of flavors and pair well with various dishes.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0025-23-13603:1": -1.0887961387634277
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
            "I can sleep well if I drink a glass of wine in the evening",
            "I like to try something new here and then",
            "My grandfather used to have a winery in Great Britain",
            "I occasionally experience mild acid reflux and prefer beverages that are gentle on the stomach"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I\u2019m actually curious about wines that taste a bit like freshly cut grass. Any specific types or brands you\u2019d recommend for that kind of flavor profile?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some wine suggestions that tastes like freshly cut grass? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For wines that exhibit the flavor profile of freshly cut grass, I highly recommend trying Sauvignon Blanc. This varietal is known for its distinctive green notes, which can include aromas and flavors reminiscent of grass, green bell pepper, and herbs. \n\n1. **Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc** - Wines from this region in New Zealand are particularly noted for their vibrant, grassy character and tropical fruit flavors. A good example is the **Cloudy Bay Sauvignon Blanc**, which showcases this profile beautifully.\n\n2. **Loire Valley Sauvignon Blanc** - French versions, such as **Sancerre** or **Pouilly-Fum\u00e9**, offer a flinty and herbaceous quality, often with a more refined acidity. Look for producers like **Domaine Vacheron** for a great option.\n\n3. **Adelaide Hills Sauvignon Blanc** - Australian Sauvignon Blancs, like those from **Petaluma**, can also provide a fresh, grassy profile with a bit more fruitiness.\n\nThese options should satisfy your craving for that unique grassy flavor!",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0017-91-09558:2": 0.2791873514652252,
            "clueweb22-en0034-40-14042:5": 0.22997985780239105
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Now, if I ask you to choose between Sauvignon Blanc, Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, which would be best for someone who sometimes has acid reflux and prefers gentle wines?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your preference for gentle wines and occasional acid reflux, I would recommend the **Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote**. Sancerre wines, particularly those made from Sauvignon Blanc, can offer a more refined acidity and are often less harsh compared to other Sauvignon Blancs. The terroir of Sancerre can produce a wine that balances crispness with a softer mouthfeel, which may be easier on your stomach. The **Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi** might also be a good option, but Sancerre is generally known for its gentler profile. Avoiding the standard Sauvignon Blanc is wise, as it can be more acidic and might trigger reflux symptoms.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0010-21-08933:3": 1.025936484336853,
            "clueweb22-en0010-21-08933:1": 0.9805951118469238,
            "clueweb22-en0010-21-08933:5": 0.9801148772239685,
            "clueweb22-en0033-06-02411:5": 0.692658543586731,
            "clueweb22-en0010-21-08933:0": 0.506373941898346,
            "clueweb22-en0020-32-08617:7": 0.41434022784233093,
            "clueweb22-en0028-07-16908:11": 0.3340359330177307,
            "clueweb22-en0010-21-08933:4": 0.2910909354686737,
            "clueweb22-en0010-21-08933:6": 0.029201313853263855
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": [
