          "text": "Given your preference for gentle wines and occasional acid reflux, I would recommend the **Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote**. Sancerre wines, particularly those made from Sauvignon Blanc, can offer a more refined acidity and are often less harsh compared to other Sauvignon Blancs. The terroir of Sancerre can produce a wine that balances crispness with a softer mouthfeel, which may be easier on your stomach. The **Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi** might also be a good option, but Sancerre is generally known for its gentler profile. Avoiding the standard Sauvignon Blanc is wise, as it can be more acidic and might trigger reflux symptoms.",
