          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Of course! Since your grandfather had a winery in Great Britain, you might appreciate wines with a story or heritage. For a relaxing evening, consider a smooth red like a Malbec or a Pinot Noir, which are known for their rich flavors and can pair well with meals or be enjoyed on their own. If you prefer white wines, a crisp Sauvignon Blanc or a buttery Chardonnay could be delightful. Let me know if you\u2019d like recommendations for specific regions or food pairings!",
