          "text": "Yes, there are wines that carry a flavor reminiscent of freshly cut grass! Sauvignon Blanc is a prime example. This aromatic white wine is known for its herbaceous and earthy notes, including lime, lemongrass, and freshly cut grass. It\u2019s a refreshing choice with a crisp, dry finish. If you\u2019re intrigued by this flavor profile, I\u2019d recommend trying a Sauvignon Blanc from New Zealand, as they often emphasize these grassy and citrusy characteristics. Let me know if you\u2019d like more specific recommendations!",
