      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, that sounds intriguing. Now, which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For someone with mild acid reflux, wines that are lower in acidity are generally gentler on the stomach. Among the options you mentioned:\n\n- **Sauvignon Blanc**: While it has a crisp and refreshing profile, it tends to be higher in acidity, which might not be ideal for acid reflux.\n- **Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi**: This wine, made from Vernaccia grapes, is described as having a luxurious texture and a mineral edge. It\u2019s likely to be less acidic than Sauvignon Blanc, making it a potentially better choice for your condition.\n- **Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote**: As a Sancerre, it\u2019s also a Sauvignon Blanc, so it shares the higher acidity typical of this grape variety.\n\nBased on your preference for beverages gentle on the stomach, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi might be the most suitable option. Enjoy it slightly chilled but not too cold to fully appreciate its flavors. Let me know if you\u2019d like more tailored suggestions!",
