          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Given your background and preferences, you might enjoy exploring Canadian wines, which are gaining international recognition for their quality and uniqueness. Natural wines like Pinard & Filles Frangine offer something different and are produced in Canada, making them both local and distinctive [DOC-2]. Canadian wineries now focus on varietals such as Pinot Noir, Cabernet Franc, Chardonnay, and Riesling, which are worth trying for their quality and regional character [DOC-2]. For wines that are gentler on the stomach and lower in sugar, consider softer oaked Chardonnays or reds like Merlot and Shiraz, as these are often better tolerated by those with mild acid reflux and tend to be less sweet [DOC-3]. If you enjoy pairing wine with dark chocolate, powerful reds or dessert wines like sherry can complement the flavors well [DOC-1]. Would you like specific Canadian winery or bottle recommendations?",
