          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "If you're seeking wines with a 'freshly cut grass' flavor, Sauvignon Blanc is the go-to varietal. Its classic aromas include grass, nettles, and green bell pepper, with the grassy notes being especially pronounced in Marlborough Sauvignon Blanc from New Zealand and in French regions like Sancerre and Pouilly-Fum\u00e9 [DOC-1][DOC-3][DOC-4]. California's Fum\u00e9 Blanc (an oaked style of Sauvignon Blanc) can also offer these herbaceous qualities. Other white wines with similar profiles include Spanish Verdejo and some cool-climate Australian Sauvignon Blancs, which may also display grassy and herbal notes [DOC-1]. For a unique twist, look for Sauvignon Blancs labeled as Fum\u00e9 Blanc or explore lesser-known regions producing this grape. Are you interested in food pairings for grassy Sauvignon Blancs?",
