          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Sauvignon Blanc is known for its high acidity, which gives it a refreshing, crisp profile but can be problematic for those with acid reflux [DOC-5]. Sancerre, such as Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, is also made from Sauvignon Blanc grapes and shares this high-acid character. Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi is a Tuscan white blend (primarily Vernaccia), which tends to be less acidic than Sauvignon Blanc but is still not classified as a low-acid wine. In general, wines from warmer climates and those with lower acidity are better tolerated by people with acid reflux, but individual reactions can vary, so some trial and error may be necessary [DOC-1][DOC-2][DOC-4]. Would you like food pairing suggestions for these wines?",
