        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Maybe later. Right now, where is oaked Chardonnay made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where is the Oaked Chardonnay wine made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "In Canada, oaked Chardonnay is produced in both Ontario and British Columbia. Featherstone Estate Winery in Ontario is a pioneer in using Canadian oak barrels for their Chardonnay, making their wine unique and highly awarded for its regional character [DOC-1]. In British Columbia, Mission Hill Winery in the Okanagan Valley is renowned for its oaked Chardonnay, which gained international acclaim after winning 'Best Chardonnay Worldwide' in 1994 [DOC-3]. These regions and wineries are excellent starting points if you're looking to explore Canadian oaked Chardonnay. Are you interested in visiting any of these wineries?",
