          "text": "Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre (such as Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote) are both celebrated for their crisp, high-acid profiles, which can be more likely to aggravate acid reflux symptoms for some people [DOC-1][DOC-4]. Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, a Tuscan white blend, may be slightly less acidic than classic Sauvignon Blancs, but all wines are inherently acidic and individual reactions can vary [DOC-1][DOC-2]. There is little scientific evidence that choosing lower-acid wines will always help with acid reflux, as personal sensitivity plays a significant role [DOC-2]. If you are prone to acid reflux, it may be best to try small amounts of each and monitor your body's response, or consider wines known for lower acidity, such as Grenache, as alternatives [DOC-3]. Would you like recommendations for lower-acid white wines?",
