          "text": "For herbal or grassy notes, focus on dry white wines\u2014these align with your goals (low sugar, gentle on reflux, weight loss, novelty). Here\u2019s what fits best:\n\n**Top Picks for Herbal/Grassy Notes**\n- **Sauvignon Blanc (especially from Loire Valley, e.g., Pouilly-Fum\u00e9):** Classic grassy, herbal, and citrus flavors. Typically dry, low in sugar, and moderate in alcohol\u2014gentle on the stomach and waistline.\n- **Albari\u00f1o:** Crisp, sometimes with subtle herbal undertones. Light, refreshing, and easy on reflux.\n- **Gr\u00fcner Veltliner:** Austrian white with signature herbal, white pepper, and green notes. Usually dry and low in alcohol.\n- **Verdejo:** Spanish white, often grassy and herbal, with a clean, dry finish.\n\n**Why These Work for You**\n- Dry = minimal sugar (supports weight loss, no sugar diet)\n- Moderate to low alcohol (better for sleep, less reflux risk)\n- Herbal/grassy profiles offer novelty and complexity\n\n**What to Avoid",
