          "user_rubrik_score": null,
          "text": "Direct answer: The herbal/grassy white wines you\u2019re considering\u2014Sauvignon Blanc, Gr\u00fcner Veltliner, Albari\u00f1o, and Verdejo\u2014are typically **medium to high in acidity**. This acidity is what gives them their freshness and signature herbal notes.\n\n**What this means for you:**\n- **Acidity & Reflux:** Higher acidity can sometimes trigger acid reflux, though individual tolerance varies. Of these, Sauvignon Blanc and Gr\u00fcner Veltliner are especially known for their zesty, crisp acidity.\n- **Gentler Options:** Albari\u00f1o and Verdejo are also fresh but can be a touch softer, especially if you seek out examples labeled as \u201cround\u201d or \u201csoft\u201d in tasting notes.\n- **Low Sugar & Weight Loss:** All remain excellent for your no-sugar and weight loss goals, as they are dry and low in residual sugar.\n\n**Recommendation:** If you\u2019re sensitive to acidity, try Albari\u00f1o or Verdejo first, or look for Sauvignon Blanc from warmer regions (like California or Chile), which tend to be less sharp.\n\nWould you",
