        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I like the idea of something gentle! But today, I\u2019m curious\u2014can you recommend wines with flavors similar to freshly cut grass?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some wine suggestions that tastes like freshly cut grass? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For wines with flavors similar to freshly cut grass, you might enjoy a Sauvignon Blanc or a Gr\u00fcner Veltliner. These crisp and refreshing whites often have notes of green apple, citrus, and grassy or herbaceous undertones, which might remind you of a spring day. If you prefer reds, a Pinot Noir with earthy and vegetal notes could also fit the bill. Would you like to explore these options further?",
          "citations": {},
