        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s great! Between Sauvignon Blanc, Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, which is easiest on someone with acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Between the three options, I would recommend the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote. This wine is known for its minerality and subtle acidity, which should be gentle on your stomach. The Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi has a slightly higher acidity level, while the Sauvignon Blanc can vary depending on the specific bottle. The Sancerre La Grande Cote is a good choice for those with acid reflux, as it tends to be smoother and less likely to irritate the stomach.",
          "citations": {},
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Sounds good\u2014thanks! Switching gears, where is oaked Chardonnay wine made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where is the Oaked Chardonnay wine made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "In Canada, oaked Chardonnay wine is primarily made in the provinces of Ontario and British Columbia. The Niagara Peninsula in Ontario and the Okanagan Valley in British Columbia are known for producing high-quality Chardonnays with oak aging, which adds a rich and complex flavor profile to the wine. You might find some excellent examples from Canadian wineries in these regions. Would you like some specific recommendations?",
          "citations": {},
