          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Between Sauvignon Blanc, Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, which of these would be best for someone like me who gets the occasional acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Based on the provided information, Sauvignon Blanc is generally high in acidity, which is often not recommended for individuals with acid reflux. While Sancerre is a style of Sauvignon Blanc, there is no specific information available regarding the acidity levels or suitability for acid reflux of Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi or Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote.",
