        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it\u2014so you don\u2019t know if Terre di Tufi is any better for reflux either? If I wanted to try something with lower acidity, are there any other white wines you would suggest that might be gentler?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For white wines that are gentler on the stomach due to lower acidity, you could consider Chardonnay, which is known to be less acidic and often described as softer. Marsanne is another option, as grapes grown in hot climates tend to develop less acidity. Additionally, Viognier and Grenache Blanc are naturally low-acid grape varieties that might be suitable.",
