        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting! Out of Sauvignon Blanc, Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, which would be best for someone with acid reflux issues?",
          "user_rubrik": "Which of these wines, the Sauvignon Blanc, the Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi, and the Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are best for someone with stomach acid reflux? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "Sauvignon Blanc and Sancerre, including Domaine Pascal Cotat Sancerre La Grande Cote, are generally known for their high acidity. Wines with high acidity may not be ideal for managing acid reflux, as you prefer beverages gentle on the stomach. Unfortunately, I don't have information on the acidity or suitability of Terruzi & Puthod Terre di Tufi for acid reflux.",
