          "text": "For acid reflux, consider dry, low-alcohol wines. Light red wines like Merlot or Shiraz are often suggested as gentler options, with some research indicating they might even reduce reflux risk. While white wine can be more acidic for some, softer, oaked whites like Chardonnay might be tolerated better. Avoid bubbly wines and sugary mixers. Always consume in moderation.",
