          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some wine suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Certainly! For wine suggestions that are gentle on the stomach, especially with mild acid reflux, consider wines known for lower acidity. Good options include Grenache, Chardonnay, Merlot, Marsanne, Cabernet Sauvignon, Shiraz, and Viognier.\n\nWines from warmer climates or aged red wines tend to be less acidic. It's generally advised to avoid high-acid varieties like Pinot Noir or Sauvignon Blanc. If you experience mild reflux, an occasional drink is usually fine, but avoid drinking close to bedtime.",
