          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Can you give me some wine suggestions that taste like freshly cut grass?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some wine suggestions that tastes like freshly cut grass? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "For wines that taste like freshly cut grass, Sauvignon Blanc is an excellent choice. This white wine is widely known for its herbaceous and green notes, particularly from regions like Austria, Germany, and France (Loire Valley). New Zealand Sauvignon Blancs also frequently exhibit this characteristic, often alongside citrus and tropical fruit notes. You might also find this profile in some Trebbiano d'Abruzzo or certain white blends like Illuminati Dino.",
