      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I don\u2019t know much about it, honestly. But how about oaked Chardonnay\u2014do they make it in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where is the Oaked Chardonnay wine made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, Canada, particularly British Columbia and Ontario, produces oaked Chardonnay. For your mild acid reflux, oaked Chardonnay is generally a better choice than unoaked. Oaked Chardonnay typically has lower acidity because it often undergoes malolactic fermentation, which converts tart malic acid into softer lactic acid. This process results in a creamier, smoother wine that is gentler on the stomach.",
          "citations": {
