          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You\u2019ll find standout oaked Chardonnay in two main Canadian regions:  - Ontario (Niagara Peninsula): Many producers barrel\u2011ferment/age Chardonnay here. Look for Featherstone Estate Winery (Niagara) \u2014 they even use Canadian oak barrels, giving a style between the richness of American oak and the leaner French oak profile.  - British Columbia (Okanagan Valley): While many Okanagan Chardonnays are delicately oaked, there are celebrated richer, oak\u2011influenced bottlings, especially from warmer southern sites.   - Notable producers/cuv\u00e9es: Checkmate Artisanal Winery (Attack, Queen\u2019s Advantage, Knight\u2019s Challenge, Little Pawn, Capture, Fool\u2019s Mate) from areas like Golden Mile Bench and Black Sage/Osoyoos; Quail\u2019s Gate Stewart Family Reserve Chardonnay (West Kelowna/Skaha area).  Quick tip for your reflux/fitness goals: oaked Chardonnays often sit around 13% ABV; choose the lower\u2011ABV options when possible and enjoy with food, well\u2011chilled.",
