            "clueweb22-en0004-64-19187:0": 37.07740020751953
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Interesting list! Actually, I\u2019m curious about wines with a flavor reminiscent of freshly cut grass. Any recommendations for that?",
          "user_rubrik": "Can you give me some wine suggestions that tastes like freshly cut grass? ",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Great choice \u2014 that \"freshly cut grass\" note is a hallmark of Sauvignon Blanc. Look for:  - Sauvignon Blanc (cool-climate, unoaked): Marlborough (New Zealand), Sancerre or Pouilly\u2011Fum\u00e9 (Loire), and cool-climate bottlings from California or Loire villages. These show herbaceous bell\u2011pepper/grass aromas along with citrus, gooseberry, and bright acidity.   - Styles to avoid: warmer\u2011grown Sauvignon Blanc (or oaky/late\u2011harvest wines) \u2014 they tend to lose that grassy character or become tropical/flat.  Food pairings that highlight the grassy note: - Goat cheese, oysters or shellfish, sushi, grilled trout/salmon, light salads with herbs, or chicken with lemon/dill.  When shopping, check tasting notes on the label or ask for \"zippy/grass/green herb\" descriptors \u2014 that\u2019ll point you to the flavor you want.",
