          "text": "short answer : avoid the sancerre and other cool - climate sauvignon blancs \u2014 they \u2019 re zippy and high \u2011 acid and more likely to aggravate reflux. details and practical tips : - sauvignon blanc ( including domaine pascal cotat sancerre la grande cote ) = high acidity \u2192 not the best for reflux. - terruzi & puthod terre di tufi \u2014 style matters. if it \u2019 s a fuller, slightly rounded or lightly oaked white ( lower perceived acidity ), it may be gentler than a sancerre ; if it \u2019 s a lean, steely italian white, it could still be acidic. check tasting notes or ask the merchant. - better choices overall : off \u2011 dry riesling, richer / warmer \u2011 climate or lightly oaked chardonnay, or softer reds like merlot \u2014 these tend to be lower in sharp acidity. - consumption tips : sip small amounts, drink with food ( fat / protein buffers acid ), avoid sparkling / high \u2011 alcohol wines, and stop if you feel symptoms. if you want, tell me the exact terruzi bottling or its tasting notes and i \u2019 ll give a",
