      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Helpful detail, thanks! Switching gears\u2014where is Oaked Chardonnay wine made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik": "Where is the Oaked Chardonnay wine made in Canada?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Oaked Chardonnay is made across Canada\u2019s two main wine-producing provinces:  - British Columbia: especially the Okanagan Valley (sub\u2011regions like Golden Mile Bench, Naramata, Skaha Bench, Osoyoos, Black Sage and Kelowna) \u2014 many producers age Chardonnay in oak, and some even use Canadian oak barrels for a distinct style.   - Ontario: the Niagara Peninsula (Niagara\u2011on\u2011the\u2011Lake and Niagara Escarpment) plus Lake Erie North Shore and Prince Edward County also produce oaked Chardonnays.  If you prefer strictly local fruit in Ontario, look for the VQA label. Want recommendations for oaked Chardonnays in Canada that are gentler on reflux (lower ABV, lighter oak)? I can suggest a few bottles available where you are.",
