          "text": "The Okanagan Valley is a lake-and-river basin region in south\u2011central British Columbia centred on Okanagan Lake and the Canadian section of the Okanagan River. Major centres include Kelowna, Vernon, Penticton and West Kelowna; the region is also the Canadian half of the cross\u2011border Okanagan Country. It\u2019s one of Canada\u2019s warmest regions and the province\u2019s main wine region, with extensive vineyards and tasting routes.  Yes \u2014 it\u2019s an excellent place to spend free time. In summer you get sandy beaches, boating and water sports on Okanagan Lake, many winery tours and tastings, golf, hiking and scenic drives. In winter nearby mountains offer ski resorts. Kelowna is a convenient, lively base with good amenities. It\u2019s roughly a 4\u20135 hour drive from Vancouver, making it accessible for a long weekend or longer stay depending on where you live.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0039-11-18724:1": 2.0626394748687744,
            "clueweb22-en0033-39-08860:10": -0.2673257291316986,
            "clueweb22-en0014-66-15187:2": -0.41881582140922546,
            "clueweb22-en0039-11-18724:0": -1.1474552154541016,
            "clueweb22-en0034-39-12406:9": -1.827610969543457
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
